xt.\n2. Handle multiple possibilities like:\n   - The answer is within a specific prefix and suffix.\n   - The answer is split across multiple parts.\n   - The answer is not enclosed in the expected prefix/suffix.\n3. Return the extracted answer or `None` if it\'s not found.\n4. Return a string with a score based on the contents of the answer.\n\nThe function will be encapsulated in a clean, well-documented function with type hints, ensuring clarity and readability.\n\n---\n\n<answer>\n\n```python\nfrom typing import Union, Optional, Any\nimport re\n\ndef extract_answer(input_text: str, prefix: str = "<answer>", suffix: str = "</answer>") -> Optional[str]:\n    """\n    Extracts the answer from the input text based on the prefix and suffix.\n    \n    Args:\n        input_text (str): The text containing the answer.\n        prefix (str): The substring to match at the beginning of the answer.\n        suffix (str): The substring to match at the end of the answer.\n        \n    Returns:\n        Optional[str]: The extracted answer, or None if not found.\n    """\n    # Handle cases where the answer is not enclosed in the specified prefix/suffix\n    # Find all occurrences of the prefix and suffix pattern\n    try:\n        # Find all matches where the prefix is before the suffix\n        matches = re.findall(r\'{}.*?{}\'.format(re.escape(prefix), re.escape(suffix)), input_text, re.DOTALL)\n        if matches:\n            # Return the last match (most recent answer)\n            return matches[-1].split(suffix)[0]\n        return None\n    except Exception as e:\n        # Handle any parsing errors\n        return None\n\ndef reward(solution_str: str, *args, **kwargs) -> float:\n    """\n    Evaluates the solution based on the extracted answer.\n    \n    Args:\n        solution_str (str): The solution string to evaluate.\n        *args: Additional arguments.\n        **kwargs: Additional keyword arguments.\n        \n    Returns:\n        float: A score between -5.0